---js
{
  layout: "layouts/base.njk",
  eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true,
  pagefindIgnore: true,
  noindex: true,
  eleventyComputed: {
    // Token shape guard (shared `pages` slot): the plugin-side preview writer
    // generates URL-safe random tokens; anything else (path separators, dots,
    // …) must never reach the output path. Missing draft or malformed token →
    // permalink false → no page preview emitted at all. Mirrors the homepage
    // preview guard, scoped to the single shared pages slot (previews.pages).
    //
    // D4 SINGLE SHARED SLOT: every standalone page shares routeKey "pages", so
    // there is exactly ONE preview page (/preview/pages/<token>/) at any time —
    // previewing page B overwrites page A's artifact (acceptable: one page is
    // edited at a time). The token rotates on every page publish.
    permalink: (data) => {
      const token = data.previews?.pages?.token;
      return typeof token === "string" && /^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$/.test(token)
        ? `/preview/pages/${token}/index.html`
        : false;
    },
    title: () => "Preview — Page",
  },
}
---
{# Null guard ONLY — Eleventy renders this template on every build even when
   the computed permalink is false (it just doesn't write the output), so
   without it the shortcode runs with null and logs a false
   "[composition] unsupported schemaVersion: undefined" warn once per build.
   schemaVersion gating stays in the shortcode per the documented split. #}
{% if previews.pages %}
<div data-preview-revision="{{ previews.pages.revision }}">
  {# Pages are FULL-PAGE compositions (hero/main/sidebar/footer, the same
     homepage-shaped multi-zone model) — the draft tree IS the full page, so
     this mirrors preview-homepage.njk exactly, just sourced from the shared
     previews.pages slot.

     Direct shortcode call — NEVER via {% include %} or renderFile (Eleventy
     3.1.2 silently drops async shortcode output inside {% include %}; see
     home.njk Tier-0 and components/render-block.njk for the canonical notes).
     The shortcode owns the schemaVersion 4 + tree gates and degrades to an
     HTML comment on invalid artifacts. #}
  {% renderCompositionTree previews.pages %}
</div>
{% endif %}
